{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"709304697713852446","content":"They see it’s been busy today and send a couple of the unseen servants from earlier around to bus tables","created_at":"2020-08-20T01:56:24.574000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"745823522831466557","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Mistah Noodles","id":"363458590461132800","is_bot":0,"username":"mistahnoodles"},"author_id":"363458590461132800","channel_id":"709304697713852446","content":"It starree so subtle Baeshra didn't  even notice her foot beginning to tap to the music in her mind. Just a gentle tap with the rhythm. That is until she began to sing...\n\"Just a swamp town lizard, living in a lonely world. She took the mightnight sub going anywhere\"\nUnsure where the song came from Baeshra looked around confused and reached for a nearby broom.\n\"Just a city spider, born and raised in London. They took the midnight sub, going anywhere.\"\nBaeshra pulled the broom to herself, not defensively but like a dance partner, the way Web would hold her during thier dances. She swept across the kitchen with her \"partner\" in tow. Baeshra spun with them into the center of the pub.\n\"A long coat in a smoky room, the smell of wine and daffodil perfume.\" \nBaeshra is enraptured with the music. She let's the music lead. Giving herself to it as she lifts the broom in a spin.\n\"For a smile he would save the world. And we'll go on and on and on and on.\"\nBaeshra lowers the broom. It's no longer her partner in this dance. She  sings into the broom as if it would make the whole town hear. \n\"Strangers fighting, up and down the island. They're just trying to survive.\" \nBaeshra's head snaps up to the ceiling as she sings, she holds the broom out from her letting it dip as her other hand reaches to the tarp over the ceiling.\n\"Torchlight people, living to find emotion, hiding somewhere in the night.\"\nBaeshra snaps back to the broom to sing into it. She starts tapping  her foot a harder as she sings , she starts point to the other patrons one at a time.\n\"Hunting hard to get my fill, everybody wants a thrill. Paying anything just to roll the dice just one more time.\"","created_at":"2020-08-20T02:45:32.238000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"745835886230634638","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Mistah Noodles","id":"363458590461132800","is_bot":0,"username":"mistahnoodles"},"author_id":"363458590461132800","channel_id":"709304697713852446","content":"Baeshra starts dancing across the room with the broom again dancing between tables and rubble. Lost in ger own world.\n\"All will win, hunger will lose, the gods will have to snoooze. But the tales will never end, we'll go on and on and on and on.\"\nBaeshra returns to the center and sings at the broom. She raises a hand several times trying to get people to sing the chorus with her.\n\"Strangers fighting, up and down the island. They're just trying to survive. Torchlight people, just living to find emotion, hiding somewhere in the night.\"\nBaeshra holds the broom differently and higher. She mimics  playing an oversized lute as her head sways side to side. Her eyes shut enjoying the moment.\n\"Don't stop believing, hold on to this feeling.  Torchlight people, dont stop believing. Hold on.\"\nBaeshra begins signing into the broom again as she climbs up onto a chair, then a stool, then finally standing in the bar itself. \n\"Torchlight people. Don't stop believing. Hold on to this feeling. Torchlight people. Don't stop!\" \nBaeshra finishes her song breathing hard. She's not sure what came over her. She's barely sure how she got onto the counter. She quickly shyly climbs down from the counter  before running out of the bar embarrassed.","created_at":"2020-08-20T02:45:35.747000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"745835900948447305","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
